# Write effective links

<h2 id="wg-083">Describe the destination in the link text</h2>

Link text must make sense on its own. Do not use “click here” or “more”. A link goes somewhere. It does not run a device action.

| Before | After |
| --- | --- |
| For file links, [click here](../formatting-content/attachments.html). | See [Attachments](../formatting-content/attachments.html) for file links. |
| [Turn off heating](../formatting-content/attachments.html) (a link that switches it off) | Select the **Turn off heating** button. |

<h2 id="link-to-a-specific-page">Link to a specific page</h2>

Link to the page that answers the question, not a section home.

| Before | After |
| --- | --- |
| Look up terms in the [style guides](../style-guides/index.html). | Look up Home Assistant words in [A to Z Technical](../style-guides/technical-a-to-z.html). |

<h2 id="wg-037">Say when a link leaves Home Assistant</h2>

Name external sites and downloads before the person selects. Never put a password or token in a link.

| Before | After |
| --- | --- |
| More | Manufacturer support page (opens another website) |
| Download | Download diagnostics (.json, 140KB) |
